so there are some new mechanics and dark  souls2 that I feel like you guys need to  know about these are things that aren't  explained in game and whether you're new  to the soul series or not these are  definitely things you want to know  before you're going in we'll start with  the simple mechanics and we'll end with  some of the more complex ones first off  you can now sprint up ladders by holding  down the sprint button tapping the  sprint button while on the ladder will  make you jump off and this is different  to Dark Souls we're tapping made you  slide down so I wonder how many lives  I'll save by telling you this simple  fact the second mechanic we're going to  talk about is the new guard break  critical attack in Dark Souls 2 if you  bash it an enemy's raised shield for  long enough then he'll go into this  guard broken animation tab r1 while he's  in this animation and you'll perform a  critical attack doing massive damage on  the topic of critical attacks parrying  has changed pressing l2 will initiate a  parry animation but you have to time it  really well in Dark Souls 2 tap l2 just  before an enemy attack hits you and if  you time it right then they'll fall flat  on their back which leaves them open for  a critical attack tap r1 while they're  in this fallen state to get the critical  hit animation tap r1 too early while  they're still falling and you'll do  regular damage which causes them to get  up immediately onto the next tip if your  dual wielding weapons you can two-hand  the one in the right hand by tapping  triangle just like in the first game but  if you wanted to hand the weapon in your  left hand then hold down triangle if  you're do wielding two weapons in the  same weapon class for example right here  I'm using two daggers then you'll enter  a dual wielding stance when you hold  down the triangle button if you press l1  and l2 you'll perform special attacks be  warned though sometimes it won't let you  enter this stance even though you have  two of the same weapon and that's  probably because you don't have high  enough stats when I figure out the exact  mechanic behind this I'll put it up on  the screen the fifth mechanic we need to  talk about is that your weapons will now  take durability damage as you progress  through a level you can track this by  looking at the red bar at the bottom of  your weapon to refill this bar and  polish up your weapon just rest a tab on  fire if this weapon reaches the very end  though then you're in trouble you've  broken your weapon and you need to  return it to the blacksmith in order to  get it fixed if you don't fix it then  it's not going to be very effective the  sixth thing we're going to talk about  revolves around this really important  maiden in majula  if you're going to talk to anyone in  majula please talk to her she gives you  your first Estus flask as well as  offering you the ability to level up  with the souls you've acquired don't do  what i did and go through the first few  levels without your Estus flask it's not  fun if you find a Nestor shard in the  world then she can give you another  Estus flask in return next is that you  can burn human effigies in the bonfire  to reduce the chance of invasion by  other players but be careful with  burning these and using these because  Dark Souls 2 becomes really really hard  when you run out of human effigies also  if you find an item called sublime bone  dust in the world then you can burn it  in the majula bonfire to make your estes  more potent more powerful the next tip  revolves around one of my favourite  items which is the pyromancy hand  pyromancy scales with both faith and  intellect so whether you're a sorcerer  or a cleric you can make use of this  item  speaking of caster builds leveling your  attunement stat will not only increase  the amount of spell slots you get it  will also increase the speed at which  you cast and while we're on the topic of  stats adaptability is a new stat that  increases your animation speeds this  includes things like chugging and Estus  flasks or crushing a life gem or raising  your shield adaptability also increases  your resistance to volatile elements in  the world like poison or cursing you  can't really go wrong with adaptability  as just leveling it up means that you  become better suited to every situation  now this next thing isn't particularly a  new mechanic but it's definitely more  common in Dark Souls 2 so I found that  when you talk to almost every NPC  exhausting their dialogue will get you  more than just story and you'll find  that if you talk to more in pcs they  will appreciate it in some way maybe  they'll give you an item or maybe  they'll move to a better location just  make sure you talk to people for example  I'm going to use this to segue into the  blacksmith who gives you a hammer if you  to it oh and also in Dark Souls 1 you  didn't have to level up your catalyst or  the spell casting weapon you used for it  to be powerful but in Dark Souls 2 make  sure you level up your catalyst with  Titan ID at the blacksmith the same goes  for your shield as these two things  become way more powerful if you level  them up do not forget to do this on a  final note I'm going to tell you the  mechanic for my new favorite thing in  the game which is torches I love the way  they look the lighting in this game is  incredible toggle your options while  standing at a bonfire to light one of  the torches you have in your inventory  each torch contributes 5 minutes of lit  time to the counter now while torches  look incredible make sure you use your  time with them carefully because they  can burn out and they can eventually  leave you in the dark and I reckon that  pretty much covers it guys I can't think  of much else if there's anything you  think I missed just write it down in the  comments I just wanted to make this  video so that you'd be equipped to  tackle Dark Souls 2 you know these  things would have taken a while to  figure out on your own so hopefully it's  a bit of a shortcut for new players  remember to Kindle the bonfire if you  liked this video and have fun dying I'll  catch you guys in the next video and I  hope you're enjoying all the content  surrounding the release of this game  there's so much content to make but so  little time anyway talk to you again  soon later Dark Souls where do I start  for the better part of a year a huge  part of my life has revolved around this  game if I could sum up how I feel about  it in one video then I wouldn't have 70  other videos dedicated to it
 

